  "changes": [
    "Remove uvloop and winloop runtime dependencies; use standard asyncio across platforms.",
    "Replace six-way HSV selection, retaining arithmetic and RGB rounding.",
    "Skip preview preparation without visualisation listeners, supporting later subscriptions.",
    "Avoid unnecessary preview flattening and uint8 copies."
  ],
  "next_candidates": [
    "DDP sends 1,042 UDP packets per frame: investigate batching/device output isolation, validating delivered frames.",
    "JSON encoding is a substantial remaining GIL cost: assess binary pixel websocket messages with frontend compatibility."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic Rainbow workload on one WSL2 host, not all effects or physical hardware/audio latency.",
    "Server CPU excludes sampler/receiver; 100% means one core.",
    "Output is rate limited. Gains mainly free CPU capacity; full websocket FPS did not materially improve.",
    "Loopback UDP can drop packets; complete-frame rates are recorded separately and malformed packets fail validation.",
    "Full preview bypasses the product cap only inside the benchmark worker.",
    "Python 3.15 uses an isolated experimental environment, including samplerate-ledfx 0.4.0. Project support remains below 3.15.",
    "Sampling includes startup/shutdown. Use unprofiled runs to compare throughput.",
    "Loop accelerators must be installed separately for optional comparisons.",
    "Native Windows comparisons exclude unused FLAC/MIDI modules whose source builds require MSVC."
